<section class="obs-faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="container obs-faq-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</span><h2 id="faq-title">Good questions, clear answers.</h2><p>Get the essentials before bringing your building data into Caldren.</p><a class="text-cta" href="{{ route('contact') }}">Ask us something else</a></div><div class="obs-faq-list"><details><summary>What data do I need to get started?</summary><p>You can add a building and enter monthly utility bills, or upload a CSV with <code>timestamp,kwh</code> readings. Seven-day forecasts need at least 14 complete days of recent hourly or sub-hourly readings with sufficient coverage.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use Caldren with only monthly bills?</summary><p>Yes. Add at least two bills to see spending and usage trends. Interval readings are required for the seven-day demand forecast.</p></details><details><summary>Are the forecasts guaranteed to be accurate?</summary><p>No. Forecasts and peak alerts are AI-assisted estimates. Caldren shows their source period and historical baseline so your team can review them against actual building conditions.</p></details><details><summary>Can my teammates use the same workspace?</summary><p>Yes. A workspace owner can invite teammates to the organization, where they can view the same portfolio and buildings.</p></details><details><summary>What happens after the 30-day trial?</summary><p>Historical data stays visible. Uploads and new forecasts are gated until demo access is activated.</p></details><details><summary>Does the $99 checkout charge a real card?</summary><p>No. The current checkout is a clearly labelled local simulation. The 4242 demo flow records a simulated $99 payment and adds one month of access without storing card details or renewing automatically.</p></details></div></div></section>

